WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.999
Hey folks, welcome back to SCP Explained.

00:00:03.999 --> 00:00:09.140
Sorry if I seem a little out of it today,
truth be told I’ve been having real trouble

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.760
sleeping lately.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.530
Perhaps it’s because I spend so much time
poring through the files of the SCP Foundation

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:21.940
Archive - There’s plenty of creatures, entities,
objects, and tales that are very effective

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.869
at making you lose sleep.

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:28.730
But none quite as effective as SCP-966.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.710
Grab yourself a pot of coffee and prop your
eyelids open with some matchsticks or tape,

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.200
because you need to stay alert if you want
to survive this one.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.640
Though when you get on the wrong side of SCP-966,
I’m sorry to tell you that your chances

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.250
of survival are extremely low.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.850
And after experiencing its primary anomalous
effects, the question of how long you’ll

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.289
even want to survive will become disturbingly
prescient.

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:57.700
Like many of our explorations into the living
nightmares that the SCP Foundation deals with

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:04.449
on a daily basis, the best way to experience
exactly what SCP-966 can do is to take a look

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:07.829
at a case study regarding one of its many
unfortunate victims.

00:01:07.829 --> 00:01:12.850
In this case, that victim is a man named Terry
Halberg from New Mexico.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:17.049
In another life, perhaps Terry would have
been an ideal candidate for a Junior Researcher

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:23.329
position at the SCP Foundation: He was a scientific-minded
truth seeker whose interests lied in the more

00:01:23.329 --> 00:01:25.600
esoteric fields of study.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.950
Namely, ghosts and aliens.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:32.840
Proving the existence of life in the stars,
and the supernatural in general, was something

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.530
he considered to be his life’s work.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:40.130
This was why he moved to New Mexico, home
of Roswell, and widely considered to be the

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:43.090
UFO Capital of the United States, in the first
place.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:47.609
There, he’d performed experiments on a wide
range of bizarre phenomena - from exploring

00:01:47.609 --> 00:01:51.670
haunted houses to obsessively watching the
sky for any anomalous activity.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:56.619
He’d become a big wig in his niche online
paranormal investigation community, and his

00:01:56.619 --> 00:02:01.439
posts on the somewhat infamous Parawatch forum
always garnered plenty of attention.

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:03.229
But Terry wanted more.

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:08.709
He wasn’t in it for the fame, or the money,
or the legions of insatiable paranormal investigator

00:02:08.709 --> 00:02:09.709
groupies.

00:02:09.709 --> 00:02:11.590
He was a true believer.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.480
He wanted a close, first-hand experience with
the supernatural.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.629
And that was exactly what he was about to
get, in addition to a very harsh lesson about

00:02:20.629 --> 00:02:22.980
being careful what you wish for.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.900
It began when he got called out to Albuquerque
for a strange case of cattle mutilation.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:32.209
For those who don’t frequent the Parawatch
forums quite as often as Terry, cattle mutilation

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:37.040
is the most common nickname for the phenomenon
of large livestock - usually cows - being

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.319
found dead with unusual mutilation patterns
on their corpses.

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:44.910
While the particulars of what exactly this
means varies from believer to believer - with

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:49.940
theories ranging from aliens to Black Helicopters
- it is widely accepted across all branches

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.689
of paranormal enthusiasts that when cattle
are being mutilated, something very strange

00:02:54.689 --> 00:02:55.780
is afoot.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:03:00.260
Terry arrived at the ranch, and with the application
of a little cash to grease the appropriate

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.720
palms, he was able to conduct a recorded interview
with the rancher.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:09.060
He was a weathered man in his early sixties,
with a somewhat frantic demeanor and profoundly

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.709
tired eyes.

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:14.569
When Terry asked him if he’d experienced
any unusual phenomena in the days leading

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:18.829
up to the cattle mutilation incident, he was
surprisingly forthcoming about the hellish

00:03:18.829 --> 00:03:21.409
conditions he’d been experiencing lately.

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:25.180
The strange experiences had been going on
for several days now.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:29.400
It all started when the rancher noticed that
a number of his cows weren’t sleeping.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.520
This isn’t the easiest thing to spot in
a cow, because cattle engage in what is known

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.640
as polyphasic sleep, where instead of sleeping
for one prolonged period like humans typically

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.730
do, they sleep in small intervals throughout
a 24 hour period.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:46.790
Cows can even sleep standing up for periods
of light rest, but during REM sleep - which

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:51.050
all mammals need for healthy functioning - they
lay down just like us.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:54.959
The problem was, in the last several days,
many of the rancher’s cows hadn’t slept

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:55.959
at all.

00:03:55.959 --> 00:04:00.280
It was after this that the rancher seemingly
began to have bizarre paranormal experiences

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.280
himself.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.700
It began with a general sense of unease and
dread, which was soon followed by a sense

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.790
of severe insomnia that left him completely
unable to sleep for the past two days.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.840
During this period, things had gotten worse.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.739
He’d experienced strange noises around his
home.

00:04:15.739 --> 00:04:21.320
Footsteps, what sounded like hushed voices,
and occasionally even what could only be identified

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.210
as a low, croaking growl.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:28.470
But it wasn’t just noises, there was also
physical evidence of some kind of intrusion.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.870
Items had been knocked over or moved.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.509
At one point, a glass of water - which had
been centralized on a stable surface - had

00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:37.729
somehow fallen off the edge and shattered.

00:04:37.729 --> 00:04:42.930
The old rancher, with a trembling voice, even
stated that he’d seen things moving in the

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.030
corners of his eyes.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:48.430
Figures, shapes, little green men…

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.630
And then, the cattle mutilation spree began.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:56.110
It may have sounded morbid, but Terry had
to use everything in his power to stop himself

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.810
from smiling from ear to ear.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:02.940
While this was a terrifying experience for
the rancher, for Terry, this was an absolutely

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.860
textbook case of paranormal experience.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.870
And here he was, the very first person to
document it all!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:15.110
It could be the next Skinwalker Ranch or Rendlesham
Forest incident, and his name would forever

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:16.349
be attached to it.

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:20.860
He asked the rancher if he could see the cow’s
body, and the rancher obliged.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:25.540
Whatever had caused this - alien, ghost, or
otherwise - had really done a number on this

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.599
cow.

00:05:26.599 --> 00:05:30.500
Good portions of its abdomen had been torn
away, with evidence of what appeared to be

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.140
biting and clawing.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.490
This poor beast had been eaten alive.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:39.690
While exploring the wounds with a magnifying
glass, a scalpel, and a large pair of tweezers,

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.060
Terry discovered something incredible.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:47.550
Something frankly unprecedented, for a cattle
mutilation case: A piece of evidence left

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:51.240
behind directly by whatever had perpetrated
this act of gruesome violence.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:57.520
A long, thin, and exceedingly sharp claw,
around twelve centimeters in length and broken

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.890
at one end.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:04.660
New Mexico’s large predators include mountain
lions, black bears, bobcats, and coyotes,

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.120
and this claw was nothing like any of those.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.690
In fact, it was nothing like Terry had ever
seen before.

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:12.270
Was this his big moment?

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:16.620
Had he discovered evidence of an entirely
new supernatural creature or a specimen of

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.410
extraterrestrial life?

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:22.550
He was practically vibrating with excitement
about this new discovery.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:26.770
After thanking and paying the rancher again,
Terry took some photos, gathered some more

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:27.920
samples, and left.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:33.430
He had everything he needed to conduct a groundbreaking
investigation into the supernatural.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:36.540
Just wait until the folks on Parawatch heard
about this…

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:41.260
In all his excitement as he drove back home
from the ranch, he never once stopped to consider

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.419
what he might be bringing back with him.

00:06:43.419 --> 00:06:45.949
But really, in the end, it didn’t even matter.

00:06:45.949 --> 00:06:50.710
From the moment he stepped onto that ranch,
Terry Halberg was already doomed.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.052
He just didn’t know it yet.

00:06:52.052 --> 00:06:57.409
He arrived home and began to record all of
his information onto one master document.

00:06:57.409 --> 00:07:02.050
He also began obsessively assembling outside
research, hoping to find similar cases that

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:04.300
he could add to this emerging pattern.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:08.370
It was a mix of phenomena from both hauntings
and alien encounters.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:13.409
Could this possibly be some form of alien
ghost - the dream find of every paranormal

00:07:13.409 --> 00:07:14.409
investigator?

00:07:14.409 --> 00:07:18.289
Terry had to still his racing heart as the
possibilities bombarded his mind.

00:07:18.289 --> 00:07:21.290
He could have been working with the paranormal
find of the century here!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:25.699
In fact, he was so excited by all this, he
didn’t even realize that he worked through

00:07:25.699 --> 00:07:27.039
the entire night.

00:07:27.039 --> 00:07:28.970
He didn’t sleep a wink.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:33.159
After all, how could you, when such important
research needed to be done?

00:07:33.159 --> 00:07:36.330
The burst of nocturnal energy felt like a
godsend.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.830
The next night, not so much.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:43.220
In the meantime, Terry had compiled his information
together enough to present it to his esteemed

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.680
paranormal colleagues on the Parawatch forums.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:50.469
They were startled and amazed by what they
were seeing and hearing, especially the taped

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.639
interview with the rancher and the mysterious
claw.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:58.599
One of Terry’s closest associates, who went
by the username Johnstation, pulled up a similar

00:07:58.599 --> 00:08:02.179
bizarre case of a Los Angeles hiker who died
in the hills.

00:08:02.179 --> 00:08:06.880
In the days before his death, his family and
friends reported him complaining about insomnia,

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.650
and experiencing an increasing state of paranoia
and distress.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:15.400
He started taking long walks across remote
trails in hopes of tiring himself out enough

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.689
to finally get some sleep, but that time never
came.

00:08:18.689 --> 00:08:22.219
When his corpse was found, it was mauled and
half-eaten.

00:08:22.219 --> 00:08:26.050
Everyone assumed that a mountain lion had
killed him, and other scavengers had fed on

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:27.900
him before his body was found.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:31.110
But now, Terry wasn’t so sure.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:35.070
The more they looked into it, the more they
found strange and unpleasant deaths connected

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:38.640
to people suffering from what seemed like
severe insomnia.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.330
Despite its debilitating effects, the only
type of insomnia that directly causes death

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:48.690
is the exceedingly rare genetic condition
Fatal Familial Inаsomnia, which couldn’t

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:52.060
account for the sheer number of deaths the
Parawatch team were finding.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:57.090
In their minds, there was only one reasonable
conclusion: The deaths weren’t the result

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.081
of the insomnia itself, but whatever was causing
it.

00:09:00.081 --> 00:09:05.470
It was only then that Terry noticed his own
inability to sleep, and his previous excitement

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.270
was gradually replaced with panic.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:11.540
At first, he tried to keep it all in proportion,
knowing that it’s easy to invent things

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:14.630
to fear when you’re in uncharted territory.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:19.980
But as the days passed and the sleep never
came, his worry became unassailable.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:24.390
Terry knew that he hadn’t just discovered
a new paranormal phenomenon; he was becoming

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:26.030
one of its victims.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:30.930
He became increasingly paranoid over the next
few days, taking constant EVP readings from

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:34.800
around his apartment in hopes of detecting
whatever was around him.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.880
There were strange noises, frightening noises.

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:38.880
He just knew it!

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.520
But little did poor Terry know, there was
a very good reason he couldn’t detect his

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:44.600
tormentors.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:49.200
While they had been in his apartment for days
now, he had no hope of ever seeing them - The

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:55.330
human eye’s spectrum of visible light is
around 380 to 750 nanometers, but the monsters

00:09:55.330 --> 00:10:00.650
who had deprived him of his ability to sleep
existed somewhere around 900.

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:04.530
They were entirely undetectable to the human
eye.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:07.570
And they were waiting for their latest meal.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:12.670
As the insomnia grew worse, Terry received
some frightening news: That rancher who he’d

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:17.340
spoken to a few days before was found dead
on his property with severe injuries comparable

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:22.450
to that of a wild animal attack - Just like
his cattle, and just like all the other strange

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:25.170
cases that the Parawatch forum had found.

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:29.970
First the insomnia, then the frightening paranormal
experiences, and then…

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:33.190
Terry felt something warm and wet trickling
down the back of his neck.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:37.160
He probably would have realized it was his
own blood, if a twenty-centimeter claw - just

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:41.830
like the one he pulled out of the dead cow
- hadn’t just pierced his brainstem.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:48.080
Terry Halberg had finally gotten what he wanted:
A first-hand experience with the supernatural.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.110
And all he had to do was die.

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:57.240
But in his defense, being saved from SCP-966
- A whole species of monsters known as the

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:01.120
Sleep Killers - is almost worse than being
killed by them.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:06.000
When they release their deadly energy pulse,
their primary anomalous effect, which induces

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:11.240
sleeplessness on anyone or anything in their
immediate 20-meter radius, the effects are

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.240
permanent.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:17.360
They essentially induce Fatal Insomnia, and
your only options are to die by their claws,

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.540
or live long enough to see your own body and
mind give out from the horrible effects of

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.450
true sleep deprivation.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:28.150
They travel in pairs, and because of their
invisibility, you never know when they’re

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:33.320
lurking around you, waiting to rob you of
your sleep and then your life.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:38.440
The Foundation currently has four specimens
in containment, but believe us, there are

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:42.330
a lot more out there, and they’re hungry.

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.510
Sleep tight...If you can.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:50.160
Now go check out “Killer Living Graffiti
SCP-1155 - Predatory Street Art” and “Waldo

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:55.390
Finds You - SCP-4885 - Find Him” for more
terrifying monsters that’ll hunt you to

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:56.370
your last breath!

